WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.206
Today is October 03, 2026.

3
00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:13.358
Overnight, Wall Street surged as soft labor data revived hopes for a Federal Reserve pause.

4
00:00:13.358 --> 00:00:19.400
The S and P 500 rose point seven three percent, leaving an unfilled opening gap.

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.780
The tech-heavy Nasdaq jumped one point one nine percent to a fresh all-time high.

6
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:32.880
Meanwhile, the Dow Jones Industrial Average added point four nine percent, rebounding near critical long-term moving averages.

7
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:39.143
September non-farm payrolls arrived at just twenty-nine thousand against forecasts of eighty-four thousand.

8
00:00:39.143 --> 00:00:44.192
Unemployment ticked up to four point two percent, while wage gains cooled.

9
00:00:44.192 --> 00:00:52.108
Concurrently, the Group of Seven announced a coordinated release of one hundred million barrels of emergency reserves, targeting diesel.

10
00:00:52.108 --> 00:00:58.640
Consequently, market odds for an October rate hike collapsed from thirty percent down to twenty-one percent.

11
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.157
Treasury yields whipsawed before settling flat.

12
00:01:02.157 --> 00:01:08.934
Equity bulls view this combination as an ideal monetary policy safety window ahead of the midterm elections.

13
00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:12.268
However, bond markets remain skeptical.

14
00:01:12.268 --> 00:01:19.927
A prominent camp cautions that the core inflation battle is far from settled, with sticky tariffs and high energy costs lingering.

15
00:01:19.927 --> 00:01:30.050
Institutional traders largely treated the Friday close as a consolidation wait-and-see stance ahead of next week’s September meeting minutes and upcoming consumer price index prints.

16
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:36.606
This macro liquidity backdrop continues to channel fresh capital directly into core enterprise hardware.

17
00:01:36.606 --> 00:01:43.505
The Philadelphia Semiconductor Index powered cleanly through its June resistance zone around twelve thousand and six.

18
00:01:43.505 --> 00:01:54.621
Morgan JPMorgan strategists emphasize that semiconductor multiples have compressed to compelling entry levels relative to forward earnings estimates, which sit thirty percent higher than summer highs.

19
00:01:54.621 --> 00:01:59.608
AI infrastructure capacity remains sold out through 2027.

20
00:01:59.608 --> 00:02:04.094
However, capital expenditure structures are evolving aggressively.

21
00:02:04.094 --> 00:02:10.932
Amazon has shifted eight billion dollars worth of Blackwell chips into an off-balance-sheet special purpose vehicle.

22
00:02:10.932 --> 00:02:18.554
This allows the cloud giant to lease compute capacity while keeping massive hardware liabilities off its primary balance sheet.

23
00:02:18.554 --> 00:02:28.542
Software equities, by contrast, remain broadly neglected due to uncertain monetization, with cybersecurity serving as the sole defensive beneficiary.

24
00:02:28.542 --> 00:02:35.025
Turning to our pivotal equity movers, Nvidia stamped an exclamation point on the AI hardware trade.

25
00:02:35.025 --> 00:02:42.991
The semiconductor titan briefly breached a five trillion dollar valuation, surging over one percent to hit a fresh all-time high.

26
00:02:42.991 --> 00:02:45.834
Fundamentals received a dual boost.

27
00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:56.103
First, the board authorized an unprecedented one hundred and fifty billion dollar stock buyback, bringing active authorizations to two hundred and thirty-five billion dollars.

28
00:02:56.103 --> 00:03:06.410
Second, management unveiled the DGX Spark 64-gigabyte architecture priced near five thousand dollars, designed to run hundred-billion-parameter models natively.

29
00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:15.699
With next-year AI chip revenues projected up seventy percent, Nvidia trades around twenty-nine times earnings, continuing to squeeze short sellers.

30
00:03:15.699 --> 00:03:24.057
Immediate support sits at its previous consolidation breakout, with institutional targets shifting toward uncharted blue-sky territory.

31
00:03:24.057 --> 00:03:31.128
Tesla also seized the spotlight, leaping four point six percent following stellar third-quarter delivery figures.

32
00:03:31.128 --> 00:03:39.608
The electric vehicle pioneer delivered four hundred and eighty-six thousand five hundred vehicles against production of four hundred and sixty-four thousand units.

33
00:03:39.608 --> 00:03:46.937
This cleared twenty-two thousand units of excess inventory, demonstrating active de-stocking and firm pricing discipline.

34
00:03:46.937 --> 00:03:53.150
Furthermore, energy storage deployments reached a robust thirteen point seven gigawatt-hours.

35
00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:57.978
Technically, the stock is testing its upper multi-month descending trendline.

36
00:03:57.978 --> 00:04:03.652
A decisive breakout above recent swing highs could trigger an extended momentum squeeze.

37
00:04:03.652 --> 00:04:09.437
Downside risk management hinges on maintaining support around the two hundred-day moving average.

38
00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:16.397
Finally, legacy consumer giant Nike delivered a stark counter-narrative, plunging to eleven-year lows.

39
00:04:16.347 --> 00:04:22.413
First-quarter revenue dropped four percent, while Greater China sales tumbled twenty-two percent.

40
00:04:22.413 --> 00:04:27.781
Forward earnings per share guidance missed Wall Street consensus by over twenty percent.

41
00:04:27.781 --> 00:04:35.391
Bank of America warned that turnaround visibility for the Jordan franchise remains completely blocked through fiscal 2028.

42
00:04:35.391 --> 00:04:40.893
Key support at multi-year cycle lows has collapsed, cautioning against bottom-fishing.

43
00:04:40.893 --> 00:04:44.901
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

44
00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:49.067
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
